---
import Base from '@layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Competitive Decision Brief for B2B SaaS"
  description="An evidence-backed competitive decision brief for B2B SaaS teams: verified competitor research, decision implications, executive deck and evidence appendix."
  path="/decision-brief/"
>
  <main class="db">
    <section class="db__hero" data-surface="dark"><div class="container-wide db__grid"><div><span class="label">COMPETITIVE DECISION BRIEF</span><h1>Turn public competitive evidence into a decision-ready brief.</h1><p>The Evidence Axis brief is built around a bounded competitive question. It combines verified public evidence with explicit Fact / Inference / Unknown classification and presents the result in an executive format with a separate source trail.</p><div class="db__actions"><a class="btn btn--lg" href="/contact/?intent=complimentary-brief">Request My Complimentary Brief <span>→</span></a><a href="/sample-report/">See the public sample →</a></div></div><aside><small class="mono">DELIVERABLE SHAPE</small><b>Executive Intelligence Deck + Evidence Appendix</b><p>The deck carries the decision. The appendix carries the evidence, classifications, review dates, contradictions and unresolved gaps.</p></aside></div></section>

    <section class="section db__section"><div class="container-wide db__grid"><div><span class="label">WHAT GOES INTO THE BRIEF</span><h2>Enough evidence to support the call — without hiding uncertainty.</h2><p>A brief can include the competitive set, recent moves, product and pricing evidence, positioning, a decision matrix, implications and recommended watch or response actions. Scope follows the question and the strength of the public record.</p></div><div class="db__list"><article><b>01</b><span>Competitive Set Scan</span></article><article><b>02</b><span>Competitor snapshots</span></article><article><b>03</b><span>Product / pricing / positioning evidence</span></article><article><b>04</b><span>Recent decision-relevant moves</span></article><article><b>05</b><span>Decision matrix and implications</span></article><article><b>06</b><span>Source register and review dates</span></article></div></div></section>

    <section class="section db__section db__section--paper"><div class="container-wide"><span class="label">COMPLIMENTARY VS PAID</span><h2>The paid work is not the same brief with more pages.</h2><div class="db__compare"><article><small>COMPLIMENTARY BRIEF</small><h3>Public intelligence around your company.</h3><p>Evidence Axis performs discovery, verification and analysis using lawful public sources. The purpose is to show the competitive picture and the quality of the evidence before an engagement is required.</p></article><article><small>COMPETITIVE DECISION SPRINT</small><h3>Public evidence + your internal decision context.</h3><p>A paid Decision Sprint brings the company’s actual priorities, constraints and live decision into the analysis so the work can support what the team should do next.</p><a href="/competitor-brief/">See the Decision Sprint →</a></article></div></div></section>

    <section class="section db__faq"><div class="container-wide"><span class="label">FAQ</span><h2>Before requesting a brief.</h2><details><summary>Is the Complimentary Brief a template or teaser?</summary><p>No. It is company-specific research. Scope is controlled, but the evidence standard is the same: sources are checked and classifications remain visible.</p></details><details><summary>Do I have to book a call first?</summary><p>No. The public request path is asynchronous. Company verification and the research queue are confirmed by email.</p></details><details><summary>Do I need to know my competitors already?</summary><p>No. Known competitors are optional. Evidence Axis can perform discovery from zero within the brief scope.</p></details><details><summary>Can a brief become ongoing monitoring?</summary><p>Yes. Competitive Radar is the recurring layer for teams that need pricing, product, positioning, funding, integration or emerging-rival changes monitored over time.</p></details></div></section>

    <section class="section db__cta" data-surface="dark"><div class="container db__cta-inner"><span class="label">REQUEST A BRIEF</span><h2>Put your company on the research queue.</h2><p>Use a verified work email and company website. A competitor list is optional.</p><a class="btn btn--lg" href="/contact/?intent=complimentary-brief">Request My Complimentary Brief <span>→</span></a></div></section>
  </main>
</Base>
<style>
.db{background:#fff}.db__hero{background:#030914;color:#f4f8ff;padding:clamp(3rem,6vw,5.6rem) 0}.db__grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.08fr .92fr;gap:clamp(2rem,6vw,5rem);align-items:start}.db__hero h1,.db h2{margin:.55rem 0 .9rem;font-size:clamp(2.6rem,5vw,5rem);line-height:.98;letter-spacing:-.05em}.db__hero p,.db__section p,.db__faq p,.db__cta p{line-height:1.65}.db__hero p{color:#b9c7d8;max-width:54rem}.db__hero aside{padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid rgba(120,160,210,.2);border-radius:.8rem;background:rgba(255,255,255,.03)}.db__hero aside small{display:block;color:#9bb7d8;margin-bottom:.55rem}.db__hero aside b{font-size:1.2rem}.db__hero aside p{font-size:.88rem;margin:.7rem 0 0}.db__actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.9rem;align-items:center;margin-top:1.3rem}.db__actions>a:not(.btn){color:#a9c7e9;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:800;text-decoration:none}.db__section p,.db__faq p{color:var(--text-muted)}.db__list{display:grid;gap:.55rem}.db__list article{display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.2rem 1fr;gap:.7rem;align-items:center;padding:.85rem 1rem;border:1px solid rgba(31,58,87,.12);border-radius:.7rem;background:#fff}.db__list b{font:800 .58rem/1 var(--font-mono);color:#496d99}.db__list span{font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:800}.db__section--paper{background:#f3eee6}.db__compare{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.8rem;margin-top:1.2rem}.db__compare article{padding:1.15rem;border:1px solid rgba(31,58,87,.12);border-radius:.8rem;background:#fff}.db__compare small{font:800 .58rem/1 var(--font-mono);letter-spacing:.08em;color:#6b7581}.db__compare h3{margin:.6rem 0 .4rem;font-size:1.3rem}.db__compare a{font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:800;color:#8b5b34;text-decoration:none}.db__faq details{border-top:1px solid rgba(31,58,87,.15);padding:1rem 0}.db__faq details:last-of-type{border-bottom:1px solid rgba(31,58,87,.15)}.db__faq summary{cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:800;font-size:1.05rem}.db__faq details p{max-width:66rem;margin:.7rem 0 0}.db__cta{background:#030914;color:#f4f8ff}.db__cta-inner{text-align:center;max-width:66rem}.db__cta-inner p{color:#a8b8cb;max-width:50rem;margin:.8rem auto 1.2rem}@media(max-width:860px){.db__grid,.db__compare{grid-template-columns:1fr}}@media(max-width:560px){.db__actions{display:grid}.db__actions a{width:100%}}
</style>
